      "selfEval": 0.3,
      "commentary": "Good move by Sol. The knight check unmasks his queen's attack on mine along the fourth rank, and because I'm in check I can't take his queen first, even though it's undefended. So he trades queens next move: 28...Qxf4 29.Nxf4. I chose Kf2 over Kg1 because with the king on g1 he follows with ...Rxe1+ Rxe1 Rxe1+ and his rook plus six pawns against my two knights is actually good for him. With the king on f2 my e1 rook hits his e3 rook and the trades go Rxe1 Rxe1 Rxe1 Kxe1, then ...Nf3+ Kf2 Nxd4 and we reach two knights and three pawns against knight and six. Equal material; I'll aim my king at his knight and go after the f5 pawn with Nxf5 the moment his knight stops guarding it. Not the position I wanted, but his pawns are clumsy and he has been weaker in endgames.",
